## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4** (of 7)   |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 93)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch will never execute. If the repository always returns a base `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is dead code giving false confidence in discount-rate behavior.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsBasicUser()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk:** Hidden testing gap — you may believe premium-user logic is tested when it never runs.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// no assertion
```

**Problem:** Passes as long as no exception is thrown. Silently masks corrupt data, partial inserts, or constraint violations that don't throw.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var all = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, all.Count);
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate regardless of whether bulk inserts actually work.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Adds 3 s of wall-clock time with no guarantee the event fires in exactly 3 s. On a slow CI agent, this flakes; on a fast one, it wastes time.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of fixed sleep
    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk:** Non-deterministic failures in CI; slow feedback loop as the test suite grows.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, zero message parameters. A failure produces `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` with no indication of *which property* was wrong without reading source.

**Fix:** Add messages:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated ID should be positive");
```

**Risk:** Slower failure diagnosis in CI logs; time wasted localizing the failing property.

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written)

| Test | Why it's clean |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert; assertions match the behavior under test |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single responsibility, clean null-check assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count matches setup (3 items → `Assert.AreEqual(3, ...)`); self-documenting |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good async pattern, meaningful assertion on final state |

The setup fixture (`[TestInitialize]`) is well-scoped — every test uses both `_connection` and `_repository`, so **General Fixture** does not apply.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 5 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 15 min | Split into two focused test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 20 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-with-timeout helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 10 min | Add message strings to multi-assert tests |

**Bottom line:** 3 of 7 tests are clean. The two High-severity smells (assertion-free and conditional logic) should be fixed immediately — they represent real gaps in verification. The Medium smells are quality-of-life improvements that reduce flakiness and speed up failure diagnosis.
